{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Gad, a troop shall troop upon him.</b> And if you ask: since he will have troops, with what will he sustain them? For that requires great wealth. Therefore it is written after it: 'מאשר שמנה לחמו' — that he will be rich more than enough, and will be able to supply food for all his troops. And if you ask: from where do we know regarding 'והוא עצמו' that he will be rich? Scripture says: 'והוא יתן מעדני מלך' — that he will be so rich that he will place upon his table every delicacy of a king. And we also find that once, the people of Laodicea needed olive oil, and a Laodicean came and took sixty myriad dinars and went to the land of Israel to buy olive oil. When he arrived there, he asked the people of the place: Is there a man here who will sell me olive oil for sixty myriad dinars at once? They said to him: Go to Gush Halav, and there you will find a Jew who can sell even more and more. He went there and found that Jew in a plowed field, with his basket in his hand, like a poor laborer. That idolater was astonished and said: Is this the one about whom they say he can sell oil for a great sum such as I have? He went away to the city, but nevertheless returned to him in the evening at the house of that Jew, and found that his servants were washing his two feet in oil, in two golden pitchers, to fulfill what is said: ״וטובל בשמן רגלו״. He asked him: Do you have oil to sell for sixty myriad dinars? He said to him: Yes. He measured out that oil for him. After he measured it for him, he said to him: If you wish to buy more, I will sell you. He said to him: I have no more money. He said to him: I will extend you credit and go with you to your place. He bought from him another one hundred and fifty myriad dinars' worth. They said about that Jew that he did not leave him a horse or a mule to hire — that he did not hire any, to bring the oil he bought from him. When he arrived at his place, they praised him for having brought oil to supply all their needs. He said to them: Do not praise anyone but this Jew, who sold me all this, and I still owe him the money. And regarding both of them it is said: ״יש מתעשר ואין כל מתרושש והון רב״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The phrase ואשר עצמו in the question appears to refer to Asher himself; the spelling follows the manuscript as given. The verse 'יש מתעשר ואין כל מתרושש והון רב' is from Ecclesiastes, unaddressed by the compiler."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:38.994883262Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}